# T-118: prettier --check has never been clean on these paths, and never
# should be — reformatting them would break something specific to each,
# not just restyle it. Named individually rather than lumped, because the
# reason differs per path.

# Probe scripts AND their captured output, committed under evidence/ so a
# ticket's own claims are re-derivable by someone who was not there
# (see CLAUDE.md's "Evidence for live-verified tickets"). The .cjs/.mjs
# probes are quoted byte-for-byte out of the ticket that specified them —
# reformatting breaks the "this is exactly what the ticket said" property
# the whole point of committing them preserves. The .json/.txt captures
# are raw output from a real run, not hand-written source; there is no
# "style" to hold them to, only a record of what actually happened.
evidence/

# reports/vision-probe/*.json is the one tracked exception inside a
# directory that's otherwise entirely gitignored (see .gitignore's own
# comment) — a corpus of raw probe output, not source. Ignoring the whole
# directory rather than just the tracked glob: nothing under reports/,
# tracked or not, is meant to be prettier-managed.
reports/

# T-089: generated by scripts/generateCssColorTable.mjs via a real
# browser's getComputedStyle() — reformatting would break byte-for-byte
# reproducibility between what the generator emits and what's committed,
# the property a re-run is checked against.
scripts/cssColorTable.json
